-- coa25-service.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 37, "Service addresses": ss 1139 to 1142
-- (lines 16252-16292 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words: -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: -- NOTHING-kind (<why>), <why> being one of: silent, list not closed,
--               includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every name below begins with the section label it implements.
--
-- FORK F1. The text carries subsections (2) and (3) of s 1139 TWICE (lines 16255-16258 and 16259-16264): two
-- versions of the section ("may carry more than one extent version", inputs/SOURCES.md). The text does not say
-- which is in force, so both are encoded under distinct names ("first text", "second text") and neither overwrites
-- the other.

§ `Part 37: companies, supplementary provisions`

§§ `Service addresses`

-- ---- s 1139: Service of documents on company ------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16253 | 1139 Service of documents on company
-- src:16254 | (1) A document may be served on a company registered under this Act by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the company's registered office.
@ref s 1139(1) Service of documents on company (src:16253-16254)
GIVEN `the body is a company registered under the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is left at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is sent by post to the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1139(1) service of the document on the company is effected` MEANS
    IF `the body is a company registered under the Companies Act 2006`
       AND (`the document is left at the company's registered office` OR `the document is sent by post to the company's registered office`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A document may be served on a company registered under this Act by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the company's registered office"

-- The FIRST text of subsections (2) and (3) (lines 16255-16258).
-- src:16255 | (2) A document may be served on an overseas company whose particulars are registered under section 1046—
-- src:16256 | (a) by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the registered address of any person resident in the United Kingdom who is authorised to accept service of documents on the company's behalf, or
-- src:16257 | (b) if there is no such person, or if any such person refuses service or service cannot for any other reason be effected, by leaving it at or sending by post to any place of business of the company in the United Kingdom.
@ref s 1139(2) Service on an overseas company, first text (src:16255-16257)
GIVEN `the overseas company's particulars are registered under s 1046` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is left at, or sent by post to, the registered address of a person resident in the United Kingdom who is authorised to accept service of documents on the company's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is no such person, or a person refuses service, or service cannot for any other reason be effected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is left at, or sent by post to, a place of business of the company in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1139(2) first text: service of the document on the overseas company is effected` MEANS
    IF NOT `the overseas company's particulars are registered under s 1046`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an overseas company whose particulars are registered under section 1046"
    ELSE IF `the document is left at, or sent by post to, the registered address of a person resident in the United Kingdom who is authorised to accept service of documents on the company's behalf`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- paragraph (a)
         ELSE IF `the document is left at, or sent by post to, a place of business of the company in the United Kingdom`
              THEN IF `there is no such person, or a person refuses service, or service cannot for any other reason be effected`
                   THEN JUST TRUE -- paragraph (b)
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if there is no such person, or if any such person refuses service or service cannot for any other reason be effected" (an "if" that is not met)
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by leaving it at, or sending it by post to"

-- src:16258 | (3) For the purposes of this section a person's “registered address” means any address for the time being shown as a current address in relation to that person in the part of the register available for public inspection.
@ref s 1139(3) "Registered address", first text (src:16258)
GIVEN `the address is for the time being shown as a current address in relation to the person in the part of the register available for public inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1139(3) first text: the address is the person's registered address` MEANS
    IF `the address is for the time being shown as a current address in relation to the person in the part of the register available for public inspection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person's “registered address” means any address for the time being shown as a current address in relation to that person in the part of the register available for public inspection"

-- The SECOND text of subsections (2) and (3) (lines 16259-16264).
-- src:16259 | (2) A document may be served on an overseas company whose particulars are registered under section 1046—
-- src:16260 | (a) by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the company’s registered address, or
-- src:16261 | (b) by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the registered address of any person resident in the United Kingdom who is authorised to accept service of documents on the company’s behalf.
@ref s 1139(2) Service on an overseas company, second text (src:16259-16261)
GIVEN `the overseas company's particulars are registered under s 1046` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is left at, or sent by post to, the company's registered address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is left at, or sent by post to, the registered address of a person resident in the United Kingdom who is authorised to accept service of documents on the company's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1139(2) second text: service of the document on the overseas company is effected` MEANS
    IF `the overseas company's particulars are registered under s 1046`
       AND (`the document is left at, or sent by post to, the company's registered address`
            OR `the document is left at, or sent by post to, the registered address of a person resident in the United Kingdom who is authorised to accept service of documents on the company's behalf`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A document may be served on an overseas company whose particulars are registered under section 1046— (a) by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the company's registered address, or (b) by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the registered address of any person resident in the United Kingdom who is authorised to accept service of documents on the company's behalf"

-- src:16262 | (3) In subsection (2) “registered address”—
-- src:16263 | (a) in relation to the overseas company, means the address for the time being registered for the company under regulations under section 1048A(1)(a);
-- src:16264 | (b) in relation to a person other than the overseas company, means any address for the time being shown as a current address in relation to that person in the part of the register available for public inspection.
@ref s 1139(3) "Registered address", second text (src:16262-16264)
GIVEN `the address is for the time being registered for the overseas company under regulations under s 1048A(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1139(3)(a) second text: the address is the registered address of the overseas company` MEANS
    IF `the address is for the time being registered for the overseas company under regulations under s 1048A(1)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in relation to the overseas company, means the address for the time being registered for the company under regulations under section 1048A(1)(a)"

-- src:16262 | (3) In subsection (2) “registered address”—
-- src:16263 | (a) in relation to the overseas company, means the address for the time being registered for the company under regulations under section 1048A(1)(a);
-- src:16264 | (b) in relation to a person other than the overseas company, means any address for the time being shown as a current address in relation to that person in the part of the register available for public inspection.
@ref s 1139(3) "Registered address", second text (src:16262-16264)
GIVEN `the address is for the time being shown as a current address in relation to the person in the part of the register available for public inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1139(3)(b) second text: the address is the registered address of a person other than the overseas company` MEANS
    IF `the address is for the time being shown as a current address in relation to the person in the part of the register available for public inspection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in relation to a person other than the overseas company, means any address for the time being shown as a current address in relation to that person in the part of the register available for public inspection"

-- Subsection (4): process on a company registered in Scotland or Northern Ireland that carries on business in England and Wales.
-- src:16265 | (4) Where a company registered in Scotland or Northern Ireland carries on business in England and Wales, the process of any court in England and Wales may be served on the company by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the company's principal place of business in England and Wales, addressed to the manager or other head officer in England and Wales of the company.
@ref s 1139(4) Process on a company registered in Scotland or Northern Ireland carrying on business in England and Wales (src:16265)
GIVEN `place of registration` IS A `Place of registration`
      `the company carries on business in England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is the process of a court in England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process is left at, or sent by post to, the company's principal place of business in England and Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process is addressed to the manager or other head officer in England and Wales of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1139(4) service of the process on the company is effected` MEANS
    IF `place of registration` EQUALS `England and Wales`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a company registered in Scotland or Northern Ireland carries on business in England and Wales"
    ELSE IF NOT `the company carries on business in England and Wales`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "carries on business in England and Wales"
         ELSE IF NOT `the document is the process of a court in England and Wales`
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the process of any court in England and Wales"
              ELSE IF `the process is left at, or sent by post to, the company's principal place of business in England and Wales`
                      AND `the process is addressed to the manager or other head officer in England and Wales of the company`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the company's principal place of business in England and Wales, addressed to the manager or other head officer in England and Wales of the company"

-- src:16266 | Where process is served on a company under this subsection, the person issuing out the process must send a copy of it by post to the company's registered office.
@ref s 1139(4) The person issuing out the process must send a copy by post to the registered office (src:16266)
GIVEN `process is served on the company under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1139(4) the duty to send a copy of the process to the registered office applies` MEANS
    IF `process is served on the company under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where process is served on a company under this subsection" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)

-- src:16266 | Where process is served on a company under this subsection, the person issuing out the process must send a copy of it by post to the company's registered office.
@ref s 1139(4) The person issuing out the process must send a copy by post to the registered office (src:16266)
GIVEN `process is served on the company under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person issuing out the process has sent a copy of it by post to the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1139(4) the person issuing out the process has complied with the duty to send a copy` MEANS
    IF NOT `process is served on the company under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not engage, so nothing is left to fail (fork F5)
    ELSE IF `the person issuing out the process has sent a copy of it by post to the company's registered office`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the person issuing out the process must send a copy of it by post to the company's registered office" (a bare "must" not done: decided at this site, fork F5)

DECLARE `s 1139 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 1139 the person issuing out the process`

DECLARE `s 1139 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 1139 send a copy of the process by post to the company's registered office`

-- src:16266 | Where process is served on a company under this subsection, the person issuing out the process must send a copy of it by post to the company's registered office.
@ref s 1139(4) The person issuing out the process must send a copy by post to the registered office (src:16266)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 1139 party` `s 1139 act`
`s 1139(4) the person issuing out the process must send a copy to the registered office` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1139 the person issuing out the process`
    MUST `s 1139 send a copy of the process by post to the company's registered office`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 1139 the person issuing out the process` BECAUSE "s 1139(4): no copy of the process was sent by post to the company's registered office"

-- Subsection (5) is a signpost to the company communications provisions (inert, reason 1: fork F2).

-- ---- s 1140: Service of documents on directors, secretaries and others -----------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1140 kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 1140 a director or secretary of a company`
    `s 1140 a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company`
    `s 1140 a person holding a position of an overseas company whose particulars are registered under s 1046`
    `s 1140 a judicial factor appointed in relation to a company in Scotland`
    `s 1140 an interim manager appointed in relation to a company under s 76 of the Charities Act 2011 or s 33 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008`
    `s 1140 a manager appointed in relation to a company under s 47 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004`
    `s 1140 another kind of person`

-- src:16270 | (2) This section applies to—
-- src:16271 | (a) a director or secretary of a company;
-- src:16272 | (aa) a person who is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company (within the meanings given by section 790C);
-- src:16273 | (b) in the case of an overseas company whose particulars are registered under section 1046, a person holding any such position as may be specified for the purposes of this section by regulations under that section;
-- src:16274 | (c) a person appointed in relation to a company as—
-- src:16275 | (i) a judicial factor (in Scotland),
-- src:16276 | (ii) an interim manager appointed under section 76 of the Charities Act 2011or section 33 of Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008 , or
-- src:16277 | (iii) a manager appointed under section 47 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004 (c. 27).
@ref s 1140(2) The persons to whom s 1140 applies (src:16270-16277)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1140 kind of person`
      `s 790C the person is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the position is specified by regulations under s 1046` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1140(2) the section applies to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1140 a director or secretary of a company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1140 a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 790C the person is a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This section applies to—" is not closed with "only"; the person is not within paragraph (aa) on the s 790C answer
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "within the meanings given by section 790C"
    WHEN `s 1140 a person holding a position of an overseas company whose particulars are registered under s 1046` THEN
        IF `the position is specified by regulations under s 1046`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "a person holding any such position as may be specified for the purposes of this section by regulations under that section"
    WHEN `s 1140 a judicial factor appointed in relation to a company in Scotland` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1140 an interim manager appointed in relation to a company under s 76 of the Charities Act 2011 or s 33 of the Charities Act (Northern Ireland) 2008` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1140 a manager appointed in relation to a company under s 47 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1140 another kind of person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This section applies to—" is not closed with "only"

DECLARE `s 1140 purpose of the document` IS ONE OF
    `s 1140 a purpose arising out of or in connection with the appointment or position, or with the company concerned`
    `s 1140 any other purpose`

-- src:16278 | (3) This section applies whatever the purpose of the document in question.
-- src:16279 | It is not restricted to service for purposes arising out of or in connection with the appointment or position mentioned in subsection (2) or in connection with the company concerned.
@ref s 1140(3) The section applies whatever the purpose of the document (src:16278-16279)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 1140 purpose of the document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1140(3) the section applies to the document` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `s 1140 a purpose arising out of or in connection with the appointment or position, or with the company concerned` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1140 any other purpose` THEN JUST TRUE -- "This section applies whatever the purpose of the document in question"

-- src:16280 | (4) For the purposes of this section a person's “registered address” means any address for the time being shown as a current address in relation to that person in the part of the register available for public inspection.
@ref s 1140(4) "Registered address" (src:16280)
GIVEN `the address is for the time being shown as a current address in relation to the person in the part of the register available for public inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1140(4) the address is the person's registered address` MEANS
    IF `the address is for the time being shown as a current address in relation to the person in the part of the register available for public inspection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person's “registered address” means any address for the time being shown as a current address in relation to that person in the part of the register available for public inspection"

-- "until the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which notice of the change is registered":
-- the day notice is registered is the first of the 14 days (fork F4), so the last day of the period is that date
-- plus 13 days.
-- src:16281 | (5) If notice of a change of that address is given to the registrar, a person may validly serve a document at the address previously registered until the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which notice of the change is registered.
@ref s 1140(5) A change of address: the address previously registered stays valid for 14 days (src:16281)
GIVEN `the date on which notice of the change of address is registered` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the document is served at the address previously registered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1140(5) the document is validly served at the address previously registered` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the document is served at the address previously registered` AT MOST (`the date on which notice of the change of address is registered` PLUS 13)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person may validly serve a document at the address previously registered until the end of the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which notice of the change is registered" (an "until" that has run out)

-- src:16282 | (6) Service may not be effected by virtue of this section at an address—
-- src:16283 | (a) if notice has been registered of the termination of the appointment in relation to which the address was registered and the address is not a registered address of the person concerned in relation to any other appointment;
-- src:16284 | (b) in the case of a person holding any such position as is mentioned in subsection (2)(b), if the overseas company has ceased to have any connection with the United Kingdom by virtue of which it is required to register particulars under section 1046.
@ref s 1140(6) When service may not be effected by virtue of s 1140 (src:16282-16284)
GIVEN `notice has been registered of the termination of the appointment in relation to which the address was registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address is a registered address of the person in relation to any other appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a position mentioned in subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the overseas company has ceased to have any connection with the United Kingdom by virtue of which it is required to register particulars under s 1046` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1140(6) service may be effected by virtue of s 1140 at the address` MEANS
    IF `notice has been registered of the termination of the appointment in relation to which the address was registered`
       AND NOT `the address is a registered address of the person in relation to any other appointment`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Service may not be effected by virtue of this section at an address— (a) if notice has been registered of the termination of the appointment in relation to which the address was registered and the address is not a registered address of the person concerned in relation to any other appointment"
    ELSE IF `the person holds a position mentioned in subsection (2)(b)`
            AND `the overseas company has ceased to have any connection with the United Kingdom by virtue of which it is required to register particulars under s 1046`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Service may not be effected by virtue of this section at an address— (b) in the case of a person holding any such position as is mentioned in subsection (2)(b), if the overseas company has ceased to have any connection with the United Kingdom"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): neither "if" of (a) and (b) holds, and the prohibition says nothing about any other case

-- src:16269 | (1) A document may be served on a person to whom this section applies by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the person's registered address.
@ref s 1140(1) Service on a director, secretary or other person to whom s 1140 applies (src:16269)
GIVEN `s 1140(2) the section applies to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the document is left at, or sent by post to, the address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1140(4) the address is the person's registered address` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1140(6) service may be effected by virtue of s 1140 at the address` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1140(1) service of the document on the person is effected` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1140(6) service may be effected by virtue of s 1140 at the address`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Service may not be effected by virtue of this section at an address"
    OTHERWISE
        IF NOT `the document is left at, or sent by post to, the address`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the person's registered address"
        ELSE IF `s 1140(2) the section applies to the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 1140(4) the address is the person's registered address` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A document may be served on a person to whom this section applies by leaving it at, or sending it by post to, the person's registered address"

-- src:16286 | (8) Nothing in this section shall be read as affecting any enactment or rule of law under which permission is required for service out of the jurisdiction.
@ref s 1140(8) No effect on any enactment or rule of law requiring permission for service out of the jurisdiction (src:16286)
GIVEN `an enactment or rule of law requires permission for service out of the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1140(8) the section affects the requirement of permission for service out of the jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `an enactment or rule of law requires permission for service out of the jurisdiction`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section shall be read as affecting any enactment or rule of law under which permission is required for service out of the jurisdiction"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative reaches only an enactment or rule of law requiring permission for service out of the jurisdiction

-- Subsection (7) is a signpost to the company communications provisions (inert, reason 1: fork F2).

-- ---- s 1141: Service addresses --------------------------------------------------------------------------
