-- src:16287 | 1141 Service addresses
-- src:16288 | (1) In the Companies Acts a “service address”, in relation to a person, means an address at which documents may be effectively served on that person.
@ref s 1141(1) "Service address" (src:16287-16288)
GIVEN `documents may be effectively served on the person at the address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1141 the address is a service address` MEANS
    IF `documents may be effectively served on the person at the address`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“service address”, in relation to a person, means an address at which documents may be effectively served on that person"

-- ---- s 1142: Requirement to give service address --------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16291 | 1142 Requirement to give service address
-- src:16292 | Any obligation under the Companies Acts to give a person's address is, unless otherwise expressly provided, to give a service address for that person.
@ref s 1142 Requirement to give service address (src:16291-16292)
GIVEN `the obligation is an obligation under the Companies Acts to give a person's address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is otherwise expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1142 the address to be given is a service address` MEANS
    IF NOT `the obligation is an obligation under the Companies Acts to give a person's address`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any obligation under the Companies Acts to give a person's address"
    ELSE IF `it is otherwise expressly provided`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless otherwise expressly provided": the provision that expressly provides otherwise decides (an "unless" once met: fork F6)
         ELSE JUST TRUE
